{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/778690-foxy-children-of-the-mother","id":778690,"title":"Foxy children of the Mother","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-02T16:51:25-08:00","id":778690,"title":"Foxy children of the Mother","content":"It might be some times before I actually play WoD again, but I've currently got an idea for a character group that just won't leave and I figure developing them can't hurt.<br /> I'm really just looking for some pointers here; which of the Mother's brood would a Kitsune be? I'm working on making a human-beast family (if that's even possible???) of the creatures and I'm not sure which of the families they fit the most. I know that they can't be the deep-ones or the raptors, which just leaves three other options.<br /> <br /> Also would twin beasts have the same hunger?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8495-peachyjams","name":"PeachyJams","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8495_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T17:16:57-08:00","id":778707,"title":"","content":"It's important to remember that the Families describe the type of nightmare a given Beast embodies rather than the particulars of their Horror, but just going off of the thematics behind kitsune lore and ordinary continuation of your process of elimination they'd ostensibly fit best with high-Satiety Eshmaki; the bulk of the attributed qualities amount to categories of deception and the Lurkers are very much built on the horror of knowing one or more parts of your experience hides something dangerous.<br /> <br /> Twin Beasts might be more likely to come from the same Family, at a stretch, but narrative convention doesn't suggest any greater incidence of shared particular supernatural appetite relative to any other broodmates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}